      ":question/problem": "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}, V = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the matrices $U$ and $V$ above. Let $X$ be a $2 \\cdot 3$ standardized observation matrix, where each row represents one observation and each column represents one feature. Given that $X = U\u03a3V^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $X$, what is the second principal component of the data?"
